        <activityName xml:lang="en">Stucco, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Stucco, at plant
used for plaster, moulds, and gypsum boards; the dust emission is included in the estimated emission inventoried in the "mining Gypsum" process;
CAS number: 010034-76-1; 
Formula: CaSO4 * 0.5 H2O; 
Synonyms: gips, gypsum, plaster of Paris, calcium sulphate hemihydrate, Kalziumsulfat halbhydrat; 
UUID: 08c050ee-36ba-3999-9fee-24321d6a6787
burning of gypsum mineral and milling of stucco
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Assumed average technology for Switzerland
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: environmental report, personal communication 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_08c050ee-36ba-3999-9fee-24321d6a6787.xml</text>
